  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{x}$ is so small that $\\mathrm{x}^3$ and higher powers of $\\mathrm{x}$ may be neglected, then $\\frac{(1+x)^{3 / 2}-\\left(1+\\frac{1}{2} x\\right)^3}{(1-x)^{1 / 2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4pVVG",
      "text": "\n$1-\\frac{3}{8} x^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jhyh9",
      "text": "\n$3 x+\\frac{3}{8} x^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pWek9",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{3}{8} x^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "QKB1U",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{8} x^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& (1-x)^{1 / 2}\\left[1+\\frac{3}{2} x+\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\frac{3}{2}-1\\right) x^2-1-3\\left(\\frac{1}{2} x\\right)-3(2)\\left(\\frac{1}{2} x\\right)^2\\right] \\\\\n& =(1-x)^{1 / 2}\\left[-\\frac{3}{8} x^2\\right]=-\\frac{3}{8} x^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
